只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"基于原版 DSH 扩展，提供项目层、用户层更完整 MCP 管理 || Extended from the original DSH code, providing more complete MCP management at both project and user levels","id":"gh:1343209811","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-project-mcp-manager","slug":"wldxiaobai/dsh-project-mcp-manager","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-desktop","dsh-plugins","mcp-manager"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"基于原版 DSH 扩展，提供项目层、用户层更完整 MCP 管理 || Extended from the original DSH code, providing more complete MCP "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"management at both project and user levels"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-project-mcp-manager"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A project-level MCP auto-loading plugin for DSH: write MCP server configs in\n`<projectRoot>/.dsh/mcp"},{"id":"p4s2","text":".yml` or `.dsh/mcp.json` and they are mounted\nautomatically (via the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"client`) whenever a dsh\nsession opens in that project. Changes to the file hot-reload into the runni"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"ng\ndsh process, and tool visibility follows the session's original project\n(`session.header.cwd`). T"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"he default\n`dsh-project-mcp-manager` bundle includes the loader and the companion\n`dsh-project-mcp-u"},{"id":"p4s6","text":"i` settings page for the web and desktop apps. The UI is\nenabled by default and can be disabled inde"},{"id":"p4s7","text":"pendently; the loader keeps working."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Capability boundary** (dsh ≥ 0.2.1-rc.2): the official client owns the\nprotocol, reconnect, tool n"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ames, resources, and server instructions. Shipped\nprofiles already mount shared MCP resource tools. "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"Official configuration is\na profile-layer Cordis patch (with that layer's own HMR) plus\n`plugin_mana"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ger`. This plugin still owns what the host does not:"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"1. Project-level discovery of `<projectRoot>/.dsh/mcp.yml`, `.dsh/mcp.json`,\nand the read-only legac"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"y `.mcp.json`.\n2. Tool visibility isolated by the session's original project\n(`session.header.cwd`)."},{"id":"p6s3","text":" `working_directory` does not retarget it.\n3. The MCP file format, the `dsh-mcp` CLI, and the settin"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"g_directory` does not retarget it.\n3. The MCP file format, the `dsh-mcp` CLI, and the settings page."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Project-file hot reload is this plugin's file watcher. It does not replace\nofficial profile HMR. **T"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ransport types are decided by the official client.**\nv0.9.x targets the dsh `0.2` line starting at 0"},{"id":"p7s3","text":".2.1-rc.2 (`engines.dsh` is\n`^0.2.1-rc.2`). Hosts on dsh 0.2.0 stay on plugin v0.8.2. Hosts still on"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"\ndsh 0.1.5 should stay on plugin v0.6.0."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"If this plugin is useful, a GitHub\nstar is appreciated.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Feature documentation lives in `docs/`, English and Chinese side by side:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- Configuration format — native YAML managed\nblock, JSON dialect, divergences from the cordis dialec"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"t.\n- Settings page — use the bundled UI, read\nthe server list, add servers (with fill from clipboard"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"), switch, remove, and\nmanage tools.\n- Configuration sources and layers — the\nseven-layer source mod"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"el, shadow priority, global vs project mounting, and the\nread-only legacy Claude Code layer.\n- `${VA"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"R}` expansion — mount-time interpolation and\nits diagnostics.\n- CLI `dsh-mcp` — scopes, write format"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"s, ownership contract.\n- Query surface — `ctx.projectMcp`, the\n`projectMcp/updated` event, exported "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"view types, and the semver contract for\nthe companion UI."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Design and release records (Chinese): dsh 0.2.1-rc.2 adaptation ·\ndsh 0.2.0-rc.2 adaptation ·\ndsh 0."},{"id":"p12s2","text":"1.6-alpha.2 adaptation plan ·\ndsh 0.1.5-rc.2 adaptation ·\ndsh 0.1.5-rc.1 adaptation ·\ndsh 0.1.2-rc.1"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" adaptation ·\nJSON config layer proposal ·\nRuntime robustness & JSON interop proposal ·\nv0.9.0 relea"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"se notes ·\nv0.8.2 release notes ·\nv0.7.2 release notes ·\nv0.7.1 release notes ·\nv0.7.0 release notes"},{"id":"p12s5","text":" ·\nv0.6.0 release notes ·\nv0.4.3 release notes ·\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **Project discovery**: the `session.header.cwd` of an active agent session,\nplus the dsh process s"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"tart directory → walk up to the nearest ancestor\ncontaining `.git` as the project root (falls back t"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"o the directory itself\nwhen there is no `.git`).\n- **Mounting**: each `(project, serverName)` pair i"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"n the project layers mounts\none `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` instance (`ctx.plugin`) on the host ct"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"x and\nregisters it into the global tool layer; multiple sessions inside the same\nproject share a sin"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"gle connection. Before a workspace is focused,\nproject-layer fibers are created only for projects wi"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"th a live session or\nthe process cwd, and they unmount after a 5 minute grace. Once the user\nfocuses"},{"id":"p14s8","text":" a workspace, only that project stays mounted and the others\nunmount immediately, so a desktop works"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"pace switch cannot leave another\nproject's tools in the global list. The catalog entry and watcher r"},{"id":"p14s10","text":"emain.\n**Every\nuser-layer row mounts exactly one instance** (global, independent of the\nnumber of pr"},{"id":"p14s11","text":"ojects) — see\nconfiguration sources and layers.\n- **Hot reload**: chokidar watches each known projec"},{"id":"p14s12","text":"t root and its `.dsh`\ndirectory (depth 1). The allow-list is that root, `.dsh`, and the three\nconfig"},{"id":"p14s13","text":" files; every other path is ignored, so the watcher does not open\n`lib/`, `src/`, or `build/` and a "},{"id":"p14s14","text":"Windows build can delete those directories\nwhile dsh is running. Edits to the **exact** config files"},{"id":"p14s15","text":" of known project\nroots — `<projectRoot>/.dsh/mcp.yml`, `<projectRoot>/.dsh/mcp.json` and\n`<projectR"},{"id":"p14s16","text":"oot>/.mcp.json` — trigger a full reconciliation after a 150 ms\ndebounce: added rows are mounted, rem"},{"id":"p14s17","text":"oved rows are unmounted, and config\nchanges are remounted. A second watcher covers the\nuser layer as"},{"id":"p14s18","text":" **exact file paths** — `~/.dsh/mcp.yml`,\n`~/.dsh/mcp.json`, `~/.dsh/profiles/<active profile>/mcp.y"},{"id":"p14s19","text":"ml` and\n`mcp.json`, and\n`$DSH_HOME/dsh-mcp.json` (the other plugin's global store; watched only so\nc"},{"id":"p14s20","text":"reating it can be diagnosed, never mounted). chokidar v5 can deliver an\nevent for a watched missing "},{"id":"p14s21","text":"file when it is created, as long as its parent\ndirectory exists — never the home directory at large."},{"id":"p14s22","text":" it is created, as long as its parent\ndirectory exists — never the home directory at large.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Security boundary"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"`stdio` lines in `.dsh/mcp.yml`, `.dsh/mcp.json` and `.mcp.json` spawn their\n`command` inside the ds"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"h host process — config files are **executable code\ncarriers**, so only add them in projects you tru"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"st. The user layers\n(`~/.dsh/mcp.yml`, `~/.dsh/mcp.json`, the profile yml and json) are executable c"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ode\ncarriers too, they just belong to your own machine: user-layer rows mount\n**globally** (one host"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"-level connection, visible to every project) and are no\nlonger fanned out per project. Lines that fa"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"il to mount or are invalid are\nskipped with a warning and do not affect other servers. Claude user-s"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"tate\nmonoliths such as `~/.claude.json` (mixing credentials with project history)\nare **no longer re"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"ad at all** as of v0.4.0."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The settings page writes the same managed files, so adding a local-command\nserver there spawns that "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"command on the host. Its routes\n(`/api/project-mcp/*`) are served on the dsh connection: whoever can"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" use the\ndsh web GUI can add and start servers through it."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
